    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 0 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first team to reach target score (typically 2000-3000 points) by melding sequences, creating canastas (7+ card sequences), and going out. Score points from melded cards plus bonuses.',
      'Turn-flow example: Players draw and discard, melding sequences of 3+ consecutive cards of same suit. Wild cards (jokers/twos) can substitute. First player to empty hand takes a morto (11-card extra hand). Team can go out after taking morto and having at least one canastra. Play ends when team goes out or cards exhausted.',
      'Scoring example: At the end of each hand both teams total the point values of their melded cards, subtract the values of cards left in hand, and apply bonuses and penalties for different types of canastras, going out, and unused mortos. Teams accumulate scores over multiple hands; when a team reaches or passes the target (normally 3000 points), the team with the higher total score wins the game..',
